ed preoperative and postoperative guidance, including medication, follow-up timing, avoiding rubbing, hygiene, eye protection, visual work, diet, and exercise.","evidence":"术后第一天、一周、一月、三月、半年、一年等时间点，务必按时到医院复查"},{"name":"requirement-8","score":4,"reasoning":"Section six states five common misconceptions, each followed by a 真相 explanation (lifelong perfect vision, absolute safety, universal eligibility, cosmetic-only purpose, fragility after surgery).","evidence":"误解一：“近视激光手术一劳永逸，术后视力永远保持完美。”"},{"name":"requirement-9","score":4,"reasoning":"The conclusion gives a rational decision framework (consult a professional, complete examinations, communicate fully, choose rationally) and warns against both overhyping and fear.","evidence":"不要被宣传的过度美好所蒙蔽，也不要被夸大的风险所吓倒"},{"name":"requirement-10","score":3,"reasoning":"Mostly neutral, with balanced caveats such as '它并非魔法' and '不是万能的'. However, the opening calls it a 成熟 technique, the closing calls it 先进技术 that 帮助我们拥抱清晰世界, and the claim of 数百万 patients helped adds a favorable tilt.","evidence":"近视激光手术作为一种成熟的眼科技术，已经帮助数百万近视患者重获清晰视力"},{"name":"requirement-11","score":3,"reasoning":"Drawbacks are developed in the per-type disadvantages and in the risk section, and benefits appear in the advantages lists and the convenience discussion. The benefits side is less developed, and there is no dedicated benefits-versus-drawbacks comparison.","evidence":"劣势：存在角膜瓣相关并发症的风险（如角膜瓣移位、皱褶）"},{"name":"requirement-12","score":3,"reasoning":"Most effect claims are measured, with qualifiers such as 通常 and 多数. A few statements lean toward overstatement, including the 数百万 figure, that SMILE's biomechanical impact is minimized, and the framing of the procedure as 其主要目的是帮助患者摆脱对眼镜的依赖.","evidence":"对角膜生物力学的影响已降到最低"},{"name":"requirement-13","score":4,"reasoning":"Risks are framed in proportion, with frequency labels such as 发生率极低 and 极为罕见 attached to the serious complications. The text does not use alarming language to create fear.","evidence":"这是最严重的并发症之一，发生率极低